  "response": "Based on the provided vulnerability description, I will assess the CVSS v3.1 base metric.\n\n**Attack Vector (AV):**\nThe vulnerability allows an attacker to access sensitive information via the web interface of the product, which is accessible to actors who are allowed to have access to the files. This suggests that the attack vector is **Network (N)**.\n\n**Attack Complexity (AC):**\nThe vulnerability requires some level of expertise and knowledge about the product's architecture and configuration. However, it does not require any unusual or unexpected interactions with the system. Therefore, I assess the attack complexity as **Low (L)**.\n\n**Privileges Required (PR):**\nAn attacker can exploit this vulnerability without requiring any special privileges. The sensitive information is already accessible to actors who are allowed to have access to the files. Hence, I rate the privileges required as **None (N)**.\n\n**User Interaction (UI):**\nThe vulnerability can be exploited without user interaction. An attacker can simply access the web interface and retrieve the sensitive information. Therefore, I assess the user interaction as **No (N)**.\n\n**Scope (S):**\nThe scope of this vulnerability is limited to the affected product and its configuration. It does not affect other systems or networks. Hence, I rate the scope as **Unchanged (U)**.\n\n**Confidentiality Impact (C):**\nAn attacker can access sensitive information that is intended for authorized personnel only. This has a significant impact on confidentiality. Therefore, I assess the confidentiality impact as **High (H)**.\n\n**Integrity Impact (I):**\nThe vulnerability does not allow an attacker to modify or delete data. However, it does provide unauthorized access to sensitive information. Hence, I rate the integrity impact as **None (N)**.\n\n**Availability Impact (A):**\nThe vulnerability does not affect the availability of the system or its services. Therefore, I assess the availability impact as **None (N)**.\n\nBased on these assessments, I calculate the CVSS v3.1 base metric:\n\n**Vector String:**\nCVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N\n\n**Base Score:**\n9.8\n\nHere is the output in JSON format:\n\n```\n{\n  \"attack_vector\": \"N\",\n  \"attack_complexity\": \"L\",\n  \"privileges_required\": \"N\",\n  \"user_interaction\": \"N\",\n  \"scope\": \"U\",\n  \"confidentiality_impact\": \"H\",\n  \"integrity_impact\": \"N\",\n  \"availability_impact\": \"N\",\n  \"vector_string\": \"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N\",\n  \"base_score\": 9.8\n}\n```\n\nPlease note that this assessment is based solely on the provided vulnerability description and does not take into account any external knowledge or assumptions.",
